{"parentUuid":"84ee2883-dbe2-4287-9421-0de3634ac0a4","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a48375ff23bdc6dbe","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZQpqy3BwuJQzZ1s3onY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TtiVe5Rgg49RK3AwjfeVyH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-4; grep -E '^\\| K-' dispositions.md | grep -E '\\| (partial|reject|merge) \\|' | cut -c1-1500"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3050,"cache_read_input_tokens":40749,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3050,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TtiVe5Rgg49RK3AwjfeVyH":{"command":"cd /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-4; grep -E '^\\| K-' dispositions.md | grep -E '\\| (partial|reject|merge) \\|' | cut -c1-1500"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfZQpqXFNonhfhTWuF8TA","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"72d45590-fa70-4dc7-b9f7-f48c041269b9","timestamp":"2026-09-30T09:46:52.866Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid":"72d45590-fa70-4dc7-b9f7-f48c041269b9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"3df03163-b1a4-40b0-8c48-bb7af7bf80f9","agentId":"a48375ff23bdc6dbe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TtiVe5Rgg49RK3AwjfeVyH","type":"tool_result","content":"| K-ARCH-2 | major | scale-down | reject | verifier: The counts (74 vs 98 members, cosmetic skills tagged 'all' or server) are accurate, but docs/06 section C item 4 records that membership means 'may be built, not must be built' and that the reference game proves use. The finding c |\n| K-ARCH-4 | major | overlap | partial | hooks-only wording applied; the owner-equals-implementer check is not added — ~cap PHY.ARCH.validation: name='Physics oracle suite: analytic & reference scenes (hooks, reference scenes and threshold proposals only; suite authorship belongs to the contract's oracle_author)'; ~cap ANM.ARCH.validation: name='Animation oracle suite: pose/compression/retarget error metrics (hooks, reference scenes and threshold proposals only; suite authorship belongs to the contract's oracle_author)'; ~cap AUD.ARCH.validation: name='Audio oracle suite: bit-exact offline render, loudness, glitch & latency (hooks, reference scenes and threshold proposals only; suite authorship belongs to the contract's oracle_author)' |\n| K-ARCH-5 | major | wrong-owner | partial | two conformance experts added and contracts re-pointed; robustness-fuzzing keeps parsers and fault campaigns — +skill foundation-conformance (expert, parent test-architect); +skill ui-text-conformance (expert, parent test-architect); new area QA.CONF Conf |\n| K-ARCH-6 | major | omission | reject | verifier: Partly wrong: BLD.CI.sealed-suites is owned by the tool skill ci-cd-automation, and C-ORCH is already frozen in M0. Coordination is a recorded emerging radar entry with a human-coordinator fallback (docs/09), so 'include in M0' an |\n| K-ARCH-8 | major | missing-contract | partial | C-REWIND added as optional consumer path; no needs_implementer — +cap NET.PRED.rewound-world-query 'Hit volumes with poses as of tick T: composite of collider history and pose history with declared consistency and memory cost per tick of history' → prediction-rollback [E]; +contract C-REWIND L3 (prediction-rollback): Rewound world queries; gameplay-systems-toolkit consumes += C-REWIND? |\n| K-ARCH-12 | minor | other | partial | first-instance arbiter wording added; a data check for named process contracts is not added — ~cap ARCH.ORG.escalation: name='Escalation tiers & decision SLAs; a non-party lead of the workstream is the first-instance arbiter of intra-workstream disputes; engine-architect decides cross-workstream disputes and disputes in which the arbitrating lead is a party' |\n| K-COMPLETE-5 | minor | omission | reject | verifier: Timezone/DST is absent, but PLAT.LIVE.events already owns time-gated activation with trusted-time as authority, so calendar/tzdata policy is an implementation detail of an existing capability rather than a framework-level ownershi |\n| K-FUTURE-2 | major | maturity-error | partial | reviewed date, as_of and max_age checked; evidence_refs typing not added — radar: as_of, max_age_days per class and reviewed dates (evidence_refs typing is not added) (partial) |\n| K-FUTURE-3 | major | omission | partial | capability and radar entry added; no new target/platform value — +cap PLAT.PAL.cloud-render-host 'Engine as cloud render host: headless GPU rendering, frame capture, low-latency hardware encode, video/input back-channel, multi-tenant GPU packing' → platform-architect [M] |\n| K-FUTURE-7 | minor | scale-down | reject | verifier: The WebGL non-goal and its measured-share revisit trigger (PLAT.WEB.audience-share) are a recorded, reasoned scope decision in docs/00 and radar, and the finding adds no new evidence beyond the general WebGPU rollout tail. |\n| K-GAMEPLAY-6 | major | scale-down | reject | verifier: The premise that the minimal profile is narrative-centric and carries VN needs is not evidenced in the data or docs, and portrait staging and text reveal are game-level content (docs/06 C.2 scopes game-specific systems out), so ma |\n| K-LEGACY-2 | major | omission | reject | verifier: Baked GI/PVS exist as E capabilities, but docs/06 B5 already records 'baked stays for low tiers', dynamic GI and GPU HZB occlusion capabilities already exist, and using the baked capabilities as stance for an anti-baked pattern is |\n| K-LEGACY-3 | major | omission | reject | verifier: Four unrelated gaps are bundled and each is partly covered (L03/CORE.JOBS.thread-model for threads, L65/L16/L66 for sleeps, blocking IO and budgeted allocation), and they are catalogue-completeness wishes rather than a major defec |\n| K-LEGACY-7 | minor | wrong-boundary | reject | verifier: L39, L18, L07 and WLD.MODEL.strategy/file-per-object already stance partitioned worlds, the renames are cosmetic, and adding the bare term 'level' to contradiction_terms would false-positive on many unrelated capability and skill  |\n| K-LEGACY-8 | minor | other | reject | verifier: CORE.OBJ.world-instances already states world-scoped state reachable only through a world handle with no current-world global and L32 stances it, so ECS singletons are already covered and the finding is a naming preference. |\n| K-NET-1 | major | dependency-error | reject | verifier: Only C-REP lacks an M2 configuration (replication is profile 'online' only); C-PREDICT, C-NETSESSION and C-HOSTAUTH are exercised at M2 by fighting-2d-rollback-client (online-rollback contains prediction-rollback, net-session and  |\n| K-NET-6 | major | scale-down | reject | verifier: The configuration facts are true, but docs/00 records a reasoned decision that input-only netcode families are separate add-ons not linked to state replication/servers, relay operation is external:backend, and lockstep/rollback so |\n| K-NET-7 | major | missing-contract | reject | verifier: Overstated: C-PREDICT already lists rewind queries and consumes C-PHYS?/C-ANIM?, NET.PRED.lagcomp is owned by prediction-rollback (so the composed query has an owner), and C-PREDICT no longer requires C-REP by a recorded decision; |\n| K-NET-11 | minor | scale-down | reject | verifier: ANM.RT.pose-history is indeed restricted to lite3d/std3d, but PHY.ARCH.rewind already covers collider history, GAM.SYS.hit-detection owns frame-data hitboxes with a prediction-rollback contributor, and frame-data hitboxes are stat |\n| K-PERF-3 | major | dependency-error | partial | gate moved to M1 and circularity broken; scale-probe precondition on freezes not added — asymptotic declaration gate moves to M1; M5 scale-content is validated by QA.SIM.mass-agents, breaking the circularity; the M1 scale-probe precondition on freezes is not added (partial) |\n| K-PERF-7 | minor | other | partial | four of five gates added — gates: M2 PRF.NET.resim-cost and PRF.MEM.size, M3 PRF.METH.energy, M4 PRF.NET.latency (M5 XR energy gate not added: one gate per capability) (partial) |\n| K-PLATFORM-6 | major | omission | partial | store axis carried by capabilities, not a platform_variants field — +cap PLAT.SVC.pc-storefronts 'PC storefront SDK adapters (Steamworks, Epic Online Services, GOG Galaxy, Microsoft Store/GDK-PC), Steam Input and overlay rules' → platform-services [E]; +cap BLD.REL.store-variants 'Per-store build variants and depots' → packaging-release-patching [E]; a store axis is carried by these capabilities, not by a platform_variants field (partial) |\n| K-PLATFORM-8 | minor | wrong-owner | reject | verifier: UI.A11Y.screen-reader and UI.TXT.ime are owned by the domain skills with platform-architect as contributor. That is the framework's standard domain-owns, platform-contributes pattern, so this is an ownership preference rather than |\n| K-PLATFORM-9 | minor | omission | reject | verifier: platform-server-host is defined as having no GPU and rhi-vulkan omits server-host. The GPU-server cases are speculative: tools configurations run on 