{"parentUuid":"3294f606-cc27-49b7-873a-5f2a67b8f04c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"dd57ce8b-c203-427b-8b55-fa55e6dd1984","agentId":"a48375ff23bdc6dbe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pn6dJLMTkWdUiK7VFgNyLn","type":"tool_result","content":"127:| Security-critical runtime code (crypto, signed artifacts, anti-rollback) is `security-runtime` (`C-SIGN`); policy stays with the process skill `security-engineering`, privacy with `privacy-data-protection`. | Six verifiers must share one envelope and trust store; a process skill cannot own code. |\n64:| Agent provenance & boundaries | emerging | program-orchestration | `ARCH.ORG.provenance` | SLSA provenance applied to agents (new) | Industry provenance standard for AI-authored code | Mandatory human review sampling per tier (ARCH.ORG.human-gates) and frozen agent authority over oracles |\n81:| Coordination of ~150 autonomous agents (program) | emerging | program-orchestration | `ARCH.ORG.ownership-ledger`, `ARCH.ORG.staffing`, `ARCH.ORG.change-requests`, `ARCH.ORG.write-sets`, `ARCH.ORG.skill-lifecycle`, `ARCH.ORG.agent-continuity`, `ARCH.ORG.delegated-planning` | No published precedent at this agent count; multi-agent coding systems (2025) | Two milestones completed without lock deadlock or lost work | Human coordinator role per workstream and mandatory human review sampling per tier (ARCH.ORG.human-gates) |\n124:| L01 | Central sequential update loop | one function calls subsystems in order each frame | Task graph of phases with derived ordering (C-FRAME) | frame-orchestration | `CORE.FRAME.access-model`, `CORE.FRAME.phases` |\n126:| L03 | Game-thread / render-thread dichotomy | named long-lived render thread | Render work as tasks in overlapping task-graph frames; dedicated threads only by ADR (thread inventory in CORE.JOBS.thread-model) | frame-orchestration | `CORE.FRAME.pipelining`, `RND.GPU.recording`, `CORE.JOBS.thread-model` |\n153:| L30 | Frame-coupled variable-timestep simulation | simulation stepped by render delta | Fixed/declared step with interpolation per C-FRAME | frame-orchestration | `CORE.FRAME.fixed-step` |\n['ARCH.ORG.ownership-ledger', 'Ownership ledger & territory locks', 'program-orchestration', 'M']\n['ARCH.ORG.agent-continuity', 'Agent continuity: lock leases with heartbeats and fencing tokens, stale-lock reclamation, mandatory task hand-off record and re-brief when an agent crashes, runs out of context or is replaced', 'program-orchestration', 'M']\n['ARCH.ORG.write-sets', 'Module/file write-set convention & shared-file protocol', 'program-orchestration', 'M', ['build-system-toolchains']]\n['ARCH.ORG.provenance', 'Per-change agent/model/task attestation in the ledger', 'program-orchestration', 'M', ['security-engineering']]\n['BLD.CI.sealed-suites', 'Sealed suites: holdouts, gate-time seeds and expected outputs readable only by oracle authors and CI runners (access class sealed:oracle); execution only inside CI, results reported as pass/fail plus failure category', 'ci-cd-automation', 'E', ['test-architect']]\n['ARCH.GOV.fitness', 'Automated architectural fitness functions (layering, dependency, contract conformance)', 'architecture-governance', 'E']\n['ARCH.ORG.sensitive-paths', \"Sensitive write sets (registry parsers, crypto, auth, sandboxes, build & CI) require a K-SEC gate plus a second agent's approval; the agent control plane (ledger, access classes, critics.json, check.py, registry, human-gates register, seeds) needs human-gate approval and a fitness function diffs it against the protected branch\", 'program-orchestration', 'E', ['security-engineering']]\n[{'id': 'C-ORCH', 'layer': 'P', 'owner': 'program-orchestration', 'name': 'Agent coordination protocol', 'summary': \"Ownership ledger with access classes; write sets by module convention (src/<skill-id>/, tools/<skill-id>/; tests owned by the test-owning skill); shared-file protocol; contributor semantics (review + change request, never direct writes); change requests; integration order and milestones; human-gate tasks; failure triage; per-change provenance; critic gates with calibration and independent adjudication; access classes per skill and per path (public | nda:<holder> | sealed:oracle); NDA work routed only to cleared agents; test write sets: tests/unit/<skill-id>/ implementer-owned; tests/acceptance/<contract-id>/ owned by the contract's oracle_author, read-only (oracle-ro) for implementers; sealed holdouts, gate-time seeds and expected outputs live under access class sealed:oracle, readable only by oracle_author agents and CI runners and never by an implementer of that contract (BLD.CI.sealed-suites, QA.AGENT.holdout); lock leases and hand-off records (ARCH.ORG.agent-continuity); work-package format for delegated planning; model lineage recorded per change.\", 'requires': [], 'universal': 'all'}]\n{'kind': 'process', 'workstream': 'governance', 'purpose': 'Turns architecture into coordinated multi-agent work: decomposes milestones into tasks by skill territory, keeps the ownership ledger and territory locks, sequences integration through vertical slices, routes contract change requests, and schedules critic gates.'}\nprogram-orchestration process","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4649f2d7-7d39-4397-8bb5-d6fc13558120","timestamp":"2026-09-30T09:48:09.147Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3294f606-cc27-49b7-873a-5f2a67b8f04c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
